mark draft

# SHELVED 2026-10-02 (base-v1-0038): it declared a top-level `get`, and names are package-global, so it shadowed list
# `get` wherever it was built. Nothing loads it; `clock` reads the time through `current-time`.

# The current time, as declarative bindings with no runtime shim: the wall clock in milliseconds, and the monotonic
# timer, which is immune to the clock being adjusted and so is the one to measure durations with. Internal: reached
# only through the public clock API.

bind wall-milliseconds
  like number
  case node
    text <Date.now()>

bind precise-milliseconds
  like number
  case node
    text <performance.now()>

task get
  take
    precise
    like boolean
    fall false
  like number

  fork test
    hook test
      read precise
    hook hold
      send back
        call precise-milliseconds
    hook miss
      send back
        call wall-milliseconds
